(2001043, 275846, 40106, '<td valign="top">there seems to be a lot of noise  in the skyline.  but i love the black and white and the rule of thirds.  i think the person ads a nice touch :) 6</td>', 'there seems to be a lot of noise  in the skyline.  but i love the black and white and the rule of thirds.  i think the person ads a nice touch :) 6', '2006-01-04 01:20:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001044, 275939, 39349, '<td valign="top">WOW! I love how you''ve captured the action without blowing out your highlights (no pun intended).</td>', 'WOW! I love how you''ve captured the action without blowing out your highlights (no pun intended).', '2006-01-04 01:20:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001054, 274853, 13688, '<td valign="top">this is much more city ish than most of the shots, but your focus is  a bit soft.  Also i''m not sure why there is a purple cast on the shot as straight black and white would have worked fine</td>', 'this is much more city ish than most of the shots, but your focus is  a bit soft.  Also i''m not sure why there is a purple cast on the shot as straight black and white would have worked fine', '2006-01-04 01:22:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001062, 275972, 49007, '<td valign="top">Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes<br/>- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Bad. Rotate so that the tracks go diagonally across the image or have them straight. Actually, I just spotted the road going diagnal. Make the rails go straight accross. The high viewpoint is a challenging composition, because we are not used to seeing things from this angle.<br/>- Is there anything that should be removed? The are several bits along the edges that draw the eye away.<br/>- Is there anything missing? A focal point. What should me eye be drawn to?<br/> <br/>What is my reaction or feelings? It doesn''t really grab me. I like high viewpoint images, because they are unusual, but there is no hook in this image.</td>', 'Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Bad. Rotate so that the tracks go diagonally across the image or have them straight. Actually, I just spotted the road going diagnal. Make the rails go straight accross. The high viewpoint is a challenging composition, because we are not used to seeing things from this angle.- Is there anything that should be removed? The are several bits along the edges that draw the eye away.- Is there anything missing? A focal point. What should me eye be drawn to? What is my reaction or feelings? It doesn''t really grab me. I like high viewpoint images, because they are unusual, but there is no hook in this image.', '2006-01-04 01:23:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2001071, 275018, 43434, '<td valign="top">There are so many elements in this photo that make it a good concept, but which have counted against it working properly.  There is so much movement happening that it is hard on the eyes, maybe croping out the first guys who is sorta face on would have helped with this.  The other main issue is the flare from the sunset is it.  it has wiped out a number of elements, that would have made the picture work. ( or as my partner says its interesting it makes you wonder what the ???? it is) :)</td>', 'There are so many elements in this photo that make it a good concept, but which have counted against it working properly.  There is so much movement happening that it is hard on the eyes, maybe croping out the first guys who is sorta face on would have helped with this.  The other main issue is the flare from the sunset is it.  it has wiped out a number of elements, that would have made the picture work. ( or as my partner says its interesting it makes you wonder what the ???? it is) :)', '2006-01-04 01:25:15.000000', NULL, 1),
