(2013374, 276467, 33535, '<td valign="top">i guess many people are not fan of that hight contrast, but i like it <br/>what i dislike is the fact that you cropped the glasses but it''s not that bad ;P<br/>though nice selfportrait, katherine *G*</td>', 'i guess many people are not fan of that hight contrast, but i like it what i dislike is the fact that you cropped the glasses but it''s not that bad ;Pthough nice selfportrait, katherine *G*', '2006-01-07 18:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2013388, 276367, 30364, '<td valign="top">I like urban decay images, especially if they''re B&amp;W and processed as sympathetically as this one.  However, I think this one is just too busy, too packed with chaotic detail, to be totally successful.  I''m thinking of the well known aphorism "Less is More" (by Ludwig Mies van der Rohe - appropriately enough, an architect).  I think my difficulty may be not so much with the scope of the scene, but with the fact that there''s no dominant element in it, so my eyes and attention wander about, not finding somewhere to settle.  The result is that I make a superficial scan and pass on.  That''s a pity, because it had the potential to be terrific.  6.</td>', 'I like urban decay images, especially if they''re B&W and processed as sympathetically as this one.  However, I think this one is just too busy, too packed with chaotic detail, to be totally successful.  I''m thinking of the well known aphorism "Less is More" (by Ludwig Mies van der Rohe - appropriately enough, an architect).  I think my difficulty may be not so much with the scope of the scene, but with the fact that there''s no dominant element in it, so my eyes and attention wander about, not finding somewhere to settle.  The result is that I make a superficial scan and pass on.  That''s a pity, because it had the potential to be terrific.  6.', '2006-01-07 18:42:34.000000', NULL, 1),
