(2025258, 276268, 9338, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the votes.  This is the highest I''ve made it so far.  Still, no ribbon.  Sigh.<br/> <br/>There were comments about the horizon a bit askew.  It''s not, actually.  Land was a bit higher on the right.  If I straightened the photo horizon on the land, then the horizontal lines of the sky would be the next thing many would notice askew.  Now if only this wasn''t a Basic Editing competition...<br/> <br/>Yes, the lights were overblown.  I guess that''s the aesthetic license I exercised.  I like the way the city "burns" with life.  The "hottest" parts are actually the night spots.<br/> <br/>The moon is actually young, not a full moon.  But the long time exposure brought forth the shadowed part.  Accidental effect but I like it.<br/> <br/>Taken from my backyard (yes, I''m lucky to have this almost every night) in Antipolo.  The city is Metro-Manila, Philippines.</td>', 'Thanks for the votes.  This is the highest I''ve made it so far.  Still, no ribbon.  Sigh. There were comments about the horizon a bit askew.  It''s not, actually.  Land was a bit higher on the right.  If I straightened the photo horizon on the land, then the horizontal lines of the sky would be the next thing many would notice askew.  Now if only this wasn''t a Basic Editing competition... Yes, the lights were overblown.  I guess that''s the aesthetic license I exercised.  I like the way the city "burns" with life.  The "hottest" parts are actually the night spots. The moon is actually young, not a full moon.  But the long time exposure brought forth the shadowed part.  Accidental effect but I like it. Taken from my backyard (yes, I''m lucky to have this almost every night) in Antipolo.  The city is Metro-Manila, Philippines.', '2006-01-11 06:20:48.000000', NULL, 0),
