(2049215, 273455, 48966, '<td valign="top">This was my favorite as well. It evoked a lot of chatter amongst the realms, both positive and negative, a sure sign that is is a powerful image! Just what one always hopes for. Congrats.</td>', 'This was my favorite as well. It evoked a lot of chatter amongst the realms, both positive and negative, a sure sign that is is a powerful image! Just what one always hopes for. Congrats.', '2006-01-17 16:30:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2049315, 274853, 49007, '<td valign="top">**** Greeting from the Critique Club ****<br/> <br/>Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes<br/>- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? The biggest problem with the composition is the huge patch of sky in the background that is washing out the colors and details. I''m assuming that you were shooting toward the sun. Looks like it''s coming from the upper right. Good leading lines of the platform. I can''t decide if a tighter crop would improve things.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? No. I would use a narrower aperature to have more in focus, especially the sign overhead.<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? No<br/>- Good use of shadows? It''s hard to tell because the image is do dull. It''s really hard to see the details because of this.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- Colors and Contrast Needs work to make the image brighter and "Pop".<br/>- Sharpness. Needs to to make it sharper. Better focus, DOF, and Unsharp Mash would help.<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? I occurs to me like a tourist snapshot. The subject is good, but the technicals aren''t quite there, yet.</td>', '**** Greeting from the Critique Club **** Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? The biggest problem with the composition is the huge patch of sky in the background that is washing out the colors and details. I''m assuming that you were shooting toward the sun. Looks like it''s coming from the upper right. Good leading lines of the platform. I can''t decide if a tighter crop would improve things.- Good use of Depth of Field? No. I would use a narrower aperature to have more in focus, especially the sign overhead. Lighting - Good use of light? No- Good use of shadows? It''s hard to tell because the image is do dull. It''s really hard to see the details because of this. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- Colors and Contrast Needs work to make the image brighter and "Pop".- Sharpness. Needs to to make it sharper. Better focus, DOF, and Unsharp Mash would help.- What is my reaction or feelings? I occurs to me like a tourist snapshot. The subject is good, but the technicals aren''t quite there, yet.', '2006-01-17 16:53:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2049378, 276290, 37893, '<td valign="top">Pretty sweet image Pidge :) Love the lines created by the flow of lights. A real colorful wonder that brings much delight to whomever sees it ;)</td>', 'Pretty sweet image Pidge :) Love the lines created by the flow of lights. A real colorful wonder that brings much delight to whomever sees it ;)', '2006-01-17 17:06:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(2051044, 276319, 14476, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Congratulations on your very fine entry in your first Challenge.  <br/> <br/>The composition of this image is excellent with the nice leading lines of the traffic and bridge taking the viewer into the bright lights of the city.  You smudged out the potential distraction of the near wall that is blue in the image.  The Santa Monica pier jutting out is a perfect foil to the bridge.  Good color, good detail. Good score.<br/> <br/>Keep up this way and you''ll be on the front page before you know it.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Congratulations on your very fine entry in your first Challenge.   The composition of this image is excellent with the nice leading lines of the traffic and bridge taking the viewer into the bright lights of the city.  You smudged out the potential distraction of the near wall that is blue in the image.  The Santa Monica pier jutting out is a perfect foil to the bridge.  Good color, good detail. Good score. Keep up this way and you''ll be on the front page before you know it.', '2006-01-17 22:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2051438, 276120, 49007, '<td valign="top">**** Greeting from the Critique Club ****<br/> <br/>Challenge<br/>- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes<br/>- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes<br/> <br/>Compostion<br/>- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Strong Composition, however I would recommend cropping the minivan from the left and between the antenna and mirror on the car on the right. I like the fireman in the foreground with his partner in the background. Nice placement.<br/>- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. The lead fireman is in focus, but everything behind him is soft. Excellent.<br/>- Good focus? Yes<br/> <br/>Lighting <br/>- Good use of light? Two issues. The reflected light for the fire engine headlights. The lead fireman is too dark to the front side. Use some fill flash our bring it up in post-processing. I like the reflections and shadows on the wet street.<br/> <br/>Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:<br/>- What is my reaction or feelings? Like someone commented below. I feel like I am there. It''s a good shot.</td>', '**** Greeting from the Critique Club **** Challenge- Relevant to the Challenge? Yes- Is subject unique (vs. unoriginal or rehashed)? Yes Compostion- Good or Bad? How can it be fixed? Strong Composition, however I would recommend cropping the minivan from the left and between the antenna and mirror on the car on the right. I like the fireman in the foreground with his partner in the background. Nice placement.- Good use of Depth of Field? Yes. The lead fireman is in focus, but everything behind him is soft. Excellent.- Good focus? Yes Lighting - Good use of light? Two issues. The reflected light for the fire engine headlights. The lead fireman is too dark to the front side. Use some fill flash our bring it up in post-processing. I like the reflections and shadows on the wet street. Aesthetics/Artistic Appeal:- What is my reaction or feelings? Like someone commented below. I feel like I am there. It''s a good shot.', '2006-01-17 23:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
